  "verification_policy": {
    "genus_mismatch": "REFUSE -- a different genus is not a naming variation",
    "species_epithet_mismatch": "FLAG, kept on disk but excluded from the usable set; this is where reclassifications and synonyms land",
    "no_binomial_in_header": "UNVERIFIABLE -- its own state, never counted as a pass; --allow-unverifiable opts it into the usable set explicitly",
    "why": "download_genome takes an accession and cannot know which organism the caller believed it to be, so a mis-resolved accession is a fully successful download of the wrong genome that enters the corpus under the spec's label with nothing downstream to contradict it"
  },
  "honest_limits": [
    "Name verification checks the organism string in the FASTA header. It catches a mis-resolved accession; it does NOT verify the assembly is the right STRAIN, nor that the sequence is what the accession claims.",
    "The binomial parser takes the first capitalised-then-lowercase word pair in the header. That matched every real example checked in this cache, but header formats vary across submitters and a miss becomes UNVERIFIABLE rather than a wrong pass.",
    "The disk estimate assumes bacterial-scale assemblies at about 6 MB each. It is not a safe guide for a eukaryotic batch, which is orders of magnitude larger.",
    "A FLAG is not a rejection and a REFUSE is not a deletion: files stay on disk for a human to adjudicate, and only the usable set is offered to the corpus builder."
  ]
}